From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:07:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Hunter bird snares and box traps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Bird snares and box traps were not implemented.

Change. Lay a bird snare or box trap (Hunter level per trap and
creature, 1-5 traps at Hunter 1/20/40/60/80); every 3 ticks a set trap
with a matching creature within 2 tiles rolls the catch on that
creature's own skilling curve at the player's Hunter level, from the
"Skilling success chart" on each creature's wiki page (out of 256, low at
level 1 / high at 99): crimson swift 100/420, golden warbler 92/400,
copper longtail 85/390, cerulean twitch 82/380, tropical wagtail 75/370,
grey chinchompa 6/268, carnivorous and black chinchompa -78/228 (the
values Mod Ash gave). The trap goes through the trapping/failing locs to
full or broken. A caught chinchompa or embertailed jerboa comes back
after 7 ticks. Check gives the loot, the trap and the XP ("You've caught
a <creature>."; the jerboa's "...or maybe not."), and only needs room for
what doesn't stack (box traps, bird snares and chinchompas stack);
Dismantle/Reset/Investigate. Five birds (crimson swift to tropical
wagtail), ferrets, embertailed jerboas (Hunter 39, 137 XP, jerboa tail)
and grey, red and black chinchompas. Server-only dbtables hunter_traps
(56004) and hunter_trap_creatures (56005; per-creature low/high/respawn
columns), rows 60172-60183, timer hunter_traps 436, own
HunterTrapPluginPack. Trap locs are the ones RuneLite's Hunter plugin
tracks. Needs the Hunter module skeleton PR.

Tests. Integration suite HunterTrapScriptTest (7): each creature's catch
curve against its wiki chart and Mod Ash's numbers, 7-tick chinchompa
respawns, lay/catch/check a crimson swift, a full inventory leaves the
trap, Check with a full inventory when the box trap and the chinchompa
stack, the level-1 trap limit.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Bird snare, Box trap, Crimson swift, Golden
warbler, Copper longtail, Cerulean twitch, Tropical wagtail, Ferret
(Hunter), Chinchompa (Hunter), Carnivorous chinchompa, Black chinchompa
(Hunter), Embertailed jerboa (levels, XP, loot, charts, respawn times,
the jerboa message), and the Mod Ash posts quoted there (bird rates
15 Feb 2022, chinchompa rates 23 Sep 2015, 3-tick attempts). Trap locs
from the cache; RuneLite Hunter plugin (BSD).

Caveats. XP where the wiki disagrees with itself (unsourced, needs a
game check): cerulean twitch 64.5 (creature page; Bird snare page says
64.6), tropical wagtail 95.2 (creature page; Bird snare 95), ferret
115.2 (creature page; Box trap 115); the creature pages' values are
used. Guesses: the ferret and jerboa catch curves (no wiki chart; the
crimson swift curve shifted to their level: 15/335 and -24/296), the
50-tick respawn of birds and ferrets, the snare attempt cadence, the
200-tick collapse, most trap messages, traps dropped on logout. Not
done: Eagles' Peak requirement, smoking and baiting, the extra
Wilderness trap, the baby chinchompa pet.

